                <pb facs="0126" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.515/2119: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-21T22:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>535. Your A–859, August 14. You are authorized, in your discretion, to inform the
                    Costa Rican Government in general in accordance with the penultimate paragraph
                    of your airgram but, rather than mentioning a specific date as the deadline,
                    with the finality which a specific date connotes, you should, if you deem it
                    advisable, inform the Costa Rican officials that the United States authorities
                    will take <pb facs="0127" n="113" xml:id="pg113"/> steps to prevent encashment
                    of the notes unless their deposit and appropriate freezing is effectuated within
                    the very near future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
